# macOS
.DS_Store

# The owner's working product spec. It carries job-search context, a threat model and
# PII-handling notes that do not belong in a public repo. Its public-safe derivatives are
# docs/architecture.md, docs/plan.md, docs/content-policy.md and docs/decisions/. This rule
# is a control, not tidiness: a stray copy must not be stageable by `git add -A`.
portfolio_product_spec.md

# Per-machine Claude Code settings. This file can hold credentials, so ignoring it is a
# SECRET control in a public repo, not tidiness. The tracked `.claude/` content is the two
# skills in .claude/skills/, which carry no configuration and no secrets.
.claude/settings.local.json
